\subsubsection*{7.3.2 Constructions: The general technique}
Before constructing function spaces and the Plotkin powerdomain through prelocales, the overall comparison diagram is summarized as follows:
\[
\begin{array}{ccc}
C(T(A,A')) & \subseteq & T(A,A') \\
\llbracket\cdot\rrbracket^0\downarrow & & \downarrow\llbracket\cdot\rrbracket \\
K(F_T(D,D')) & \cong_{\mathrm{dual}} C(K\Omega(F_T(D,D'))) & \subseteq K\Omega(F_T(D,D')).
\end{array}
\]
The following numbered steps explain how the ingredients are obtained.

p128-b1.tex:
\begin{enumerate}
\setcounter{enumi}{5}
\item \textbf{Completeness for \(\vee\)-primes.} Show that \(\llbracket\cdot\rrbracket^0\) is order-reflecting.
\item \textbf{Definability for \(\vee\)-primes.} Show that \(\llbracket\cdot\rrbracket^0\) is surjective.
\item \textbf{Completeness.} The interpretation function \(\llbracket\cdot\rrbracket\) itself is order-reflecting.
\end{enumerate}

