\textit{Proof of Step 15.} This is a diagram of bifinite domains and Scott-continuous functions, so checking compact elements suffices. A compact element of \(\operatorname{spec}(T(A,A'))\) is generated by a term \(a\in C(T(A,A'))\). Its image under \(\tau_A\) is the compact element generating \(\llbracket a\rrbracket^0_{T(A,A')}\); after applying \(I\), the same term generates the corresponding compact element in \(T(B,B')\). Step 12 gives the desired equality after applying \(F_T(e,e')\).

\subsubsection*{7.3.3 The function space construction}
We write \((A\Rightarrow B)\) for the set of functions mapping all of \(A\) into \(B\).

p131-b1.tex:
\textbf{Axioms and rules for function space.}
\[
\begin{array}{lll}
(\to-\wedge) & (a\to\bigwedge_{i\in I}a'_i)\approx\bigwedge_{i\in I}(a\to a'_i),\\
(\to-\vee-l) & ((\bigvee_{i\in I}a_i)\to a')\approx\bigwedge_{i\in I}(a_i\to a'),\\
(\mathrm{dist}) & a\wedge(b\vee c)\approx(a\wedge b)\vee(a\wedge c),\\[1mm]
(\to-\vee-r) & C(a)\Rightarrow (a\to\bigvee_{i\in I}a'_i)\approx\bigvee_{i\in I}(a\to a'_i),\\
(\to-\preceq) & b\preceq a, a'\preceq b'\Rightarrow (a\to a')\preceq(b\to b'),\\
(\to-C) & \text{finite joinable families }(a_i\to a'_i)\text{ are declared }\vee\text{-prime.}
\end{array}
\]
More explicitly, the last rule mirrors Definition 4.2.2: if each \(a_i,a'_i\) is \(\vee\)-prime and every finite consistency test has a finite witness, then \(C(\bigwedge_{i\in I}(a_i\to a'_i))\).

p134-b1.tex:
\textbf{Axioms and rules for the Plotkin powerlocale.}
\[
\begin{array}{lll}
(\Box-\wedge) & \Box(\bigwedge_{i\in I}a_i)=\bigwedge_{i\in I}\Box a_i, & (\Box-0)\quad \Box0=0,\\
(\Diamond-\vee) & \Diamond(\bigvee_{i\in I}a_i)=\bigvee_{i\in I}\Diamond a_i, & (\Diamond-1)\quad \Diamond1=1,\\
(\Box-\vee) & \Box(a\vee b)\preceq \Box a\vee\Diamond b, & (\Diamond-\wedge)\quad \Box a\wedge\Diamond b\preceq\Diamond(a\wedge b),\\
(\mathrm{dist}) & a\wedge(b\vee c)\approx(a\wedge b)\vee(a\wedge c).&
\end{array}
\]
\[
\begin{array}{ll}
(P-\preceq) & a\preceq b\Rightarrow \Box a\preceq\Box b\text{ and }\Diamond a\preceq\Diamond b,\\
(P-C) & \text{if all }a_i\text{ are }\vee\text{-prime and }I\ne\emptyset,\text{ then }C(\Box(\bigvee_{i\in I}a_i)\wedge\bigwedge_{i\in I}\Diamond a_i).
\end{array}
\]
Distributivity is required explicitly. The useful derived identities are
\[
\begin{aligned}
(D1)\quad &\Box(a\vee b)\approx \Box a\vee(\Box(a\vee b)\wedge\Diamond b),\\
(D2)\quad &\Box a\wedge\Diamond b\approx \Box a\wedge\Diamond(a\wedge b).
\end{aligned}
\]
Soundness is routine from the interpretation.
